{"files": [{"id": 60293158, "name": "can-21-3217_figure_s4_suppsf4.pptx", "size": 124277475, "is_link_only": false, "download_url": "https://ndownloader.figshare.com/files/60293158", "supplied_md5": "0b431eeb0a4b502e4c5f6b9e209b5fd6", "computed_md5": "0b431eeb0a4b502e4c5f6b9e209b5fd6", "mimetype": "application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.presentationml.presentation"}], "folder_structure": {}, "authors": [{"id": 15099353, "full_name": "Weijia Cai", "first_name": "Weijia", "last_name": "Cai", "is_active": false, "url_name": "_", "orcid_id": "0000-0003-1469-8991"}, {"id": 13146777, "full_name": "Mai Q. Nguyen", "first_name": "Mai Q.", "last_name": "Nguyen", "is_active": false, "url_name": "_", "orcid_id": ""}, {"id": 15099347, "full_name": "Nicole A. Wilski", "first_name": "Nicole A.", "last_name": "Wilski", "is_active": false, "url_name": "_", "orcid_id": "0000-0003-0285-0853"}, {"id": 15073093, "full_name": "Timothy J. Purwin", "first_name": "Timothy J.", "last_name": "Purwin", "is_active": false, "url_name": "_", "orcid_id": "0000-0002-7053-8039"}, {"id": 15084703, "full_name": "M\u00e9gane Vernon", "first_name": "M\u00e9gane", "last_name": "Vernon", "is_active": false, "url_name": "_", "orcid_id": "0000-0002-0953-6819"}, {"id": 392395, "full_name": "Manoela Tiago", "first_name": "Manoela", "last_name": "Tiago", "is_active": false, "url_name": "_", "orcid_id": ""}, {"id": 14940036, "full_name": "Andrew E. Aplin", "first_name": "Andrew E.", "last_name": "Aplin", "is_active": false, "url_name": "_", "orcid_id": "0000-0002-2734-3244"}], "custom_fields": [{"name": "ARTICLE ABSTRACT", "value": "Melanomas frequently harbor activating NRAS mutations. However, limited advance has been made in developing targeted therapy options for patients with NRAS mutant melanoma. MEK inhibitors (MEKi) show modest efficacy in the clinic and their actions need to be optimized. In this study, we performed a genome-wide CRISPR-Cas9\u2013based screen and demonstrated that loss of phosphoinositide-dependent kinase-1 (PDPK1) enhances the efficacy of MEKi. The synergistic effects of PDPK1 loss and MEKi was validated in NRAS mutant melanoma cell lines using pharmacologic and molecular approaches. Combined PDPK1 inhibitors (PDPK1i) with MEKi suppressed NRAS mutant xenograft growth and induced gasdermin E\u2013associated pyroptosis. In an immune-competent allograft model, PDPK1i+MEKi increased the ratio of intratumoral CD8+ T cells, delayed tumor growth, and prolonged survival; the combination treatment was less effective against tumors in immune-deficient mice. These data suggest PDPK1i+MEKi as an efficient immunostimulatory strategy against NRAS mutant melanoma.\nTargeting PDPK1 stimulates antitumor immunity and sensitizes NRAS mutant melanoma to MEK inhibition, providing rationale for the clinical development of a combinatorial approach for treating patients with melanoma.", "settings": {"validations": {"min_length": 10, "max_length": 10000}, "placeholder": "ARTICLE ABSTRACT"}, "field_type": "textarea", "order": null, "is_mandatory": false}], "figshare_url": "https://aacr.figshare.com/articles/figure/Supplementary_Figure_from_A_Genome-Wide_Screen_Identifies_PDPK1_as_a_Target_to_Enhance_the_Efficacy_of_MEK1_2_Inhibitors_in_i_NRAS_i_Mutant_Melanoma/30860485", "download_disabled": false, "description": "Supplementary Figure from A Genome-Wide Screen Identifies PDPK1 as a Target to Enhance the Efficacy of MEK1/2 Inhibitors in <i>NRAS</i> Mutant Melanoma", "funding": "NIH", "funding_list": [{"id": 29591, "title": "NIH", "grant_code": "", "funder_name": null, "is_user_defined": 1}, {"id": 85601, "title": "Dr. Miriam and Sheldon G. Adelson Medical Research Foundation", "grant_code": "", "funder_name": null, "is_user_defined": 1}, {"id": 335318, "title": "NCI", "grant_code": "", "funder_name": null, "is_user_defined": 1}], "version": 1, "status": "public", "size": 124277475, "created_date": "2025-12-11T13:40:46Z", "modified_date": "2025-12-11T13:40:46Z", "i